# Hungry Box - line-ending policy
#
# Why this exists:
#   This repository is developed on Windows inside OneDrive with
#   core.autocrlf=true and no repository policy. Git applied a
#   machine-specific CRLF conversion on checkout, which produced
#   phantom "modified" entries in git status even though the stored
#   content was byte-identical.
#
# The policy:
#   text=auto  Git detects text vs binary. Text is stored with LF.
#   eol=lf     The working tree also uses LF, on every OS.
#
# LF is the correct choice here: this is a Node/TypeScript repository
# and npm, ESLint, Prettier (endOfLine defaults to lf), Vite, NestJS
# and Prisma all expect LF. No file tracked in this repository needs
# CRLF. This file overrides core.autocrlf, so line endings are now
# deterministic regardless of each developer's Git settings.

# Default for every path: auto-detect, store LF, check out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Text formats tracked in this repository, declared explicitly so they
# never depend on Git's binary auto-detection heuristic.
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.mts           text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.svg           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.prisma        text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.example       text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.prettierrc     text eol=lf
.prettierignore text eol=lf
.nvmrc          text eol=lf

# Binary: stored byte-for-byte, never line-ending normalized.
# "binary" is shorthand for -text -diff. No binary file is tracked
# today; these cover the formats this project will receive - product
# and category imagery for the catalogue, and partner KYC uploads.
# favicon.svg is intentionally absent: SVG is XML text and is handled
# above.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.webp          binary
*.avif          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff2         binary
*.woff          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
